# The repo-root tools, one name per line — the single list.
#
# Two readers consume this file and neither keeps its own copy:
#   * install.sh links each name into ~/.local/bin (and chmods it), and
#     refuses to run when the repo root holds a tool this file omits;
#   * tests/test_install_sh.py parses it and drives
#     `install.sh --check-tools`, so the test and the installer share one
#     rule instead of restating it.
#
# A new tool at the repo root means one added line here. Anything with an
# extension (foo.py, install.sh) is a library or a script rather than a PATH
# tool, and this file is data — so the scan needs no hand-kept ignore list.
chaos-drill
decommission
dns-check
dns-watch
feed-fresh
journal-receipt
loop-heartbeat
metric-alert
new-project
ntfy-notify
pi-backup
pi-doctor
pipeline-check
prom-dash
project-guard
ram-mode
release-watch
service-probe
staleness
